[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 1 — entry points.** The `.so` exports exactly one: `colourblind`. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m three lowest-level functions (`Protanopia`, `Deuteranopia`, `Tritanopia`) are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `static`, so they are *not* separately reachable across the FFI boundary; the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m only way to drive them is `colourblind` with the matching discriminant. Each
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m discriminant is therefore treated as its own low-level entry point below, so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m matrices are exercised directly rather than only through one convenience call.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 2 — `cb_impairment` mode (the one runtime option).** `switch` in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `colourblind` distinguishes exactly 3 valid values: `cbProtanopia` (0),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `cbDeuteranopia` (1), `cbTritanopia` (2). Out-of-range values are in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `ERRORS.md`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 3 — input value shape.** The code has no size/count/format/byte-order
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m parameters (it takes 3 scalar `float*`), so the shapes it distinguishes are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m purely the `f32` value classes that change the arithmetic outcome. From the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m expressions actually present (`mulss`, `addss`, `subss` on `f32`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | shape | why the C treats it differently |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------|-------------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | ordinary normals in `[0,1]` | the intended sRGB domain, no special rounding |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | large normals near `±FLT_MAX` | products/sums overflow to `±inf` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | subnormals & `±FLT_MIN` | products underflow to subnormal or `±0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | exact `+0.0` / `-0.0` | sign-of-zero rules: `(+0) + (-0) = +0`, `(-0) + (-0) = -0`, `x - x = +0`; the `-`-coefficient rows (`P_BR`, `D_BR`, `T_GR`) flip zero signs |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `±inf` | `inf * 0 -> QNaN`, `inf - inf -> QNaN`, else `inf` propagates |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | quiet NaN with a non-default payload | SSE forwards an operand's payload, so the exact payload bits are observable in the output |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | signalling NaN | SSE quiets it (sets mantissa MSB) while preserving sign+payload |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | mixed classes across R/G/B | selects *which* operand SSE forwards; the `dst`-before-`src` priority makes the result depend on which of R/G/B is the NaN |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | negative normals | exercises the negative coefficients and `subss` sign handling |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 4 — pointer shape.** Distinct pointers vs. aliased (`R==G==B`, and each
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pair), and unaligned pointers. `movss` is alignment-agnostic, and the C reads
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m all three inputs into locals *before* the first store — a real behavioural
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m contract a translation can break.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 5 — build/feature configuration.** `translation/Cargo.toml` declares
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **no `[features]` table**, so `default` is the only feature combination that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exists; `cargo check/test --no-default-features` is the only other spelling and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compiles the identical code. `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no options or `#ifdef`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m either — one C configuration. Verified by `translation/check_features.sh`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is **no binary/driver target** in either build (CMake declares only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `add_library(... SHARED)`, Cargo only `crate-type = ["cdylib"]`), so there is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stdout to compare.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## The table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Cross-product of axis 2 × axis 3/4, pruned to combinations the C distinguishes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is driven through the exported `colourblind` symbol of **both** `.so`s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m via `libloading`, with **many randomized inputs per row** (fixed-seed SplitMix64
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m PRNG, 20 000 iterations per row for value rows), and asserts the three output
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `f32`s match **bit-for-bit** (`to_bits()`), so NaN payload and zero sign are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compared too.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | #   | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-----|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C1  | `colourblind` / `cbProtanopia` (0) | random normals in `[0,1]` (the sRGB domain) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C2  | `colourblind` / `cbDeuteranopia` (1) | random normals in `[0,1]` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C3  | `colourblind` / `cbTritanopia` (2) | random normals in `[0,1]` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C4  | all 3 modes | random normals in `[-1,1]` (negative coefficients / `subss` sign paths) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C5  | all 3 modes | uniformly random bit patterns restricted to finite values (full binade sweep, any exponent) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C6  | all 3 modes | fully unrestricted uniformly random 32-bit patterns (mixes normals, subnormals, zeros, infs, quiet + signalling NaNs across R/G/B independently) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C7  | all 3 modes | all 8 sign combinations of exact zeros `(±0, ±0, ±0)` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C8  | all 3 modes | all 125 combinations of `{-inf, -0.0, +0.0, +inf, 1.0}^3` (boundary cross-product incl. `inf*0` and `inf-inf`) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C9  | all 3 modes | subnormal / tiny inputs: cross-product of `{±f32::MIN_POSITIVE, ±smallest subnormal, ±1e-40, ±0}` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C10 | all 3 modes | huge inputs: cross-product of `{±f32::MAX, ±f32::MAX/2, ±1e38, ±1.0}` (overflow to `inf`) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C11 | all 3 modes | one channel is a quiet NaN with a randomized non-default payload, other two ordinary normals — each of the 3 channel positions (checks *which* operand SSE forwards) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C12 | all 3 modes | one channel is a **signalling** NaN with randomized payload, others normal — each of the 3 positions (checks SSE quieting) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C13 | all 3 modes | two or three channels are NaN simultaneously with *distinct* payloads (checks the `dst`-before-`src` forwarding priority) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C14 | all 3 modes | pointers fully aliased: `R == G == B` (load-all-then-store contract) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C15 | all 3 modes | pointers partially aliased: `R==G`, `R==B`, `G==B` (three sub-cases) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C16 | all 3 modes | unaligned `float*` (offset 1, 2, 3 bytes into a byte buffer) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C17 | all 3 modes | repeated in-place application (output fed back as input, 64 iterations) — the composed pipeline a real consumer runs, where per-call rounding error accumulates | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C18 | all 3 modes | mode switched between calls on the same buffers (0→1→2→0…), interleaving the matrices over accumulating state | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C19 | `colourblind`, all 3 modes | integer-valued and exactly-representable inputs (`0,1,2,...,255`, `0.5`, `0.25`) — exact-arithmetic paths where rounding is trivial | [x] |
