[1m1. The test harness was blind (found first, and it was masking everything).[22m [38;5;10mcargo test[0m builds integration-test binaries but does [3mnot[23m rebuild a [38;5;10mcdylib[0m. My first harness [38;5;10mdlopen[0med [38;5;10mtarget/release/libcolourblind_lib.so[0m directly, so the tests were comparing the C against a stale Rust build. I proved this by mutating [38;5;10mP_RG[0m from [38;5;10m0.829…[0m to [38;5;10m0.5[0m — a gross error — and still getting 36/36 passes. The harness now shells out to [38;5;10mcargo build --lib[0m and asserts [38;5;10mmtime(.so) >= mtime(src/lib.rs)[0m before loading. Re-running the same mutation then failed 18 of 36 tests.[0m[0m
