[1m2. A real translation bug: misaligned pointer dereference[22m ([38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m C16 / [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m E10). The C compiles each access to [38;5;10mmovss[0m, which has no alignment requirement, so the C accepts an unaligned [38;5;10mfloat*[0m and returns a correct result. The Rust used plain [38;5;10m*p[0m, which is UB on a misaligned pointer: release happened to work, but debug aborted the process with [38;5;10mmisaligned pointer dereference … thread caused non-unwinding panic[0m. C returns a value, Rust kills the process — a hard divergence. Fixed with [38;5;10mread_unaligned[0m/[38;5;10mwrite_unaligned[0m, which is identical codegen on the aligned path.[0m[0m
